### SafeOps API: Phase 2 manual tests (VS Code "REST Client" extension)
### Click "Send Request" above each request. Run the three logins first; later requests reuse their tokens.
### Target: Docker stack via nginx. For local uvicorn, change to http://localhost:8000/api

@base = http://localhost:8080/api
@password = Demo@1234

# @name worker
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "worker@demo.com", "password": "{{password}}" }

###
# @name supervisor
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "supervisor@demo.com", "password": "{{password}}" }

###
# @name admin
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "admin@demo.com", "password": "{{password}}" }

###
@w = {{worker.response.body.access_token}}
@s = {{supervisor.response.body.access_token}}
@a = {{admin.response.body.access_token}}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------- Reference data
GET {{base}}/locations
Authorization: Bearer {{w}}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------- Worker dashboard
# Expect score 90: PPE 80 (gloves overdue), training 100
GET {{base}}/dashboard/worker
Authorization: Bearer {{w}}

### Security check: supervisors get 403 on the worker dashboard
GET {{base}}/dashboard/worker
Authorization: Bearer {{s}}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------- Report an incident (JSON payload + photo)
# @name newIncident
POST {{base}}/incidents
Authorization: Bearer {{w}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----SafeOps

------SafeOps
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="payload"

{"title": "Pallet slipped off forklift forks", "description": "Pallet slid off while turning into aisle 3. Nobody hurt.", "category": "near_miss", "severity": "high", "occurred_at": "2026-10-01T09:30:00Z", "location_id": 1}
------SafeOps
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="photos"; filename="sample-photo.jpg"
Content-Type: image/jpeg

< ./docs/sample-photo.jpg
------SafeOps--

### Validation check: expect 422 with per-field errors (title too short, injury without details)
POST {{base}}/incidents
Authorization: Bearer {{w}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----SafeOps

------SafeOps
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="payload"

{"title": "x", "description": "Something happened here", "category": "other", "severity": "low", "occurred_at": "2026-10-01T09:30:00Z", "injury_occurred": true}
------SafeOps--

### ---------------------------------------------------------------- Report an anonymous hazard
# Response has "reporter": null, and nothing in the database links it to the worker
# @name newHazard
POST {{base}}/hazards
Authorization: Bearer {{w}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----SafeOps

------SafeOps
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="payload"

{"category": "blocked_exit", "description": "Fire exit by the loading dock blocked by pallets again.", "severity": "high", "is_anonymous": true}
------SafeOps--

### Security check: a text file renamed .jpg is rejected (422, field "photos")
POST {{base}}/hazards
Authorization: Bearer {{w}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----SafeOps

------SafeOps
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="payload"

{"category": "other", "description": "Testing the upload filter.", "severity": "low"}
------SafeOps
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="photos"; filename="photo.jpg"
Content-Type: image/jpeg

<script>alert(1)</script>
------SafeOps--

### ---------------------------------------------------------------- Visibility rules
# Worker: own named reports only (scope "own")
GET {{base}}/incidents
Authorization: Bearer {{w}}

### Supervisor: their department (scope "department")
GET {{base}}/incidents?status=reported
Authorization: Bearer {{s}}

### Admin: everything, with filters and search
GET {{base}}/incidents?severity=critical&q=press
Authorization: Bearer {{a}}

### Supervisor opens the new incident
GET {{base}}/incidents/{{newIncident.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{s}}

### Supervisor sees the anonymous hazard, without a reporter
GET {{base}}/hazards/{{newHazard.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{s}}

### Evidence photo (same visibility rules as the report)
GET {{base}}/attachments/{{newIncident.response.body.attachments[0].id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{s}}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------- Notifications
GET {{base}}/notifications/unread-count
Authorization: Bearer {{s}}

###
GET {{base}}/notifications
Authorization: Bearer {{s}}

###
POST {{base}}/notifications/read-all
Authorization: Bearer {{s}}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------- Emergency mode
# contacts_configured is false until EMERGENCY_CONTACTS is set in .env
GET {{base}}/emergency
Authorization: Bearer {{w}}

### Sends a critical in-app alert to supervisors and admins (rate limited: 5 per minute)
POST {{base}}/emergency/alert
Authorization: Bearer {{w}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "emergency_type": "fire", "notes": "Smoke from the baler", "location_id": 1 }
